  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday Night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1051 AM CDT Wed Jun 3 2026\n\nThis great stretch of weather will continue through Saturday. The\nupper-level ridge will shift and start to breakdown, and with\nsoutherly flow in place, we will see some increase in cloud cover\nboth Friday and Saturday. With dew points slowly rising along with\nwarming air temperatures, heat index values this weekend will\napproach the upper 80s to low 90s, so keep this in mind if you\nhave any outdoor plans this weekend. Rain and storm chances \nreturn to the forecast in earnest Sunday with a 40-50% chance of\nscattered storms. This trend will continue through most of next\nweek. Storm activity will be mostly confined to the peak heating \nhours of the day with no organized severe threat on the horizon \nat this time. There will be instances of higher rain/storm \nchances, mainly Monday and Tuesday, as a series of weak shortwaves\nrotate around the ridge. Rain chances those days creep up to the \n50-70% range.",
